# Development Workflow

## Project Setup

AiTrainer is an Android application using the Gradle build system. The project follows standard Android development practices.

## Key Configuration Files
- [build.gradle](mdc:build.gradle): Project-level build configuration
- [app/build.gradle](mdc:app/build.gradle): App-module build configuration
- [settings.gradle](mdc:settings.gradle): Gradle settings
- [gradle.properties](mdc:gradle.properties): Gradle properties

## Building the Application

### Prerequisites
- Android Studio
- JDK 8 or higher
- Android SDK with minimum API level as specified in app/build.gradle

### Steps
1. Clone the repository
2. Open the project in Android Studio
3. Sync Gradle files
4. Build the project using the "Build" menu or Gradle tasks
5. Run on a physical device for best pose detection results (emulators may have limited camera support)

## Development Notes

- ML Kit dependencies are specified in app/build.gradle
- Camera permissions must be granted at runtime
- Pose detection works best in well-lit environments
- The project uses both Java and Kotlin code

## Current Status

The project maintenance has stopped with the latest version being the hot_fix branch.
